! C22-6578 PROBLEM 3.8, "NORMALIZED FLOATING-POINT VECTORS FROM VFL
! DATA", printed pp.31-32 (PDF 32-33), read in the ink.
!
!   "Given a string of 25 fields beginning at STRNG.  Each field
!   contains an integer with the description (D, 48, 6).  Write a
!   program to: (a) Change each number Nk into a normalized
!   floating-point number Fk.  (b) Create the sum of squares of Fk,
!   then take the square root.  (c) Divide each Fk by the square root,
!   and store in FLOAT through FLOAT+24.0.  (d) The sum of the squares
!   of the resultant set of floating-point numbers should now be unity
!   (barring a small round-off error)."
!
!   Method 1
!       NORMV   Z, SUM
!               LX, $1, XW1
!               LX, $2, XW2
!       LOOP    LCV(V+I)(D, 48,6), 0.48($1), 68
!       EPLUS   E+I, 48                 'number is now unnormalized FP integer
!               ST(N), 0($2)
!               *(N), $L
!               +, SUM
!               ST(U), SUM
!               CBR+, $2, LOOP          '$2 will be refilled on exit
!               SRT, ROOT
!       LOOP2   L(N), 0($2)
!               /, ROOT
!               ST(U), 0($2)
!               CB+, $2, LOOP2
!               BEW, $
!       XW1     XW, STRNG, 25, $
!       XW2     XW, FLOAT, 25, $
!       SUM     DRZ(N), (1)
!       ROOT    DRZ(N), (1)
!
! The twenty printed statements are the deck's first twenty, as printed.
! STRNG and FLOAT are the deck's.
!
! ASSEMBLED WITH ASM=strap2: strap_asm.py refuses "+, SUM" and "/, ROOT"
! (decks/problem_3_bare_op_symbol_dds.strap).
!
! WHAT EACH STATEMENT IS, with the page of the rule:
!   LCV(V+I)(D, 48,6), 0.48($1), 68.  LOAD CONVERTED, decimal to binary,
!     progressive indexing code 1.  Reference Manual printed p.29: "In
!     progressive indexing, the value field ... of the index specified
!     by I, is used as the effective address ... Subsequent to this
!     use ... the address part ... of the instruction is added to the
!     value field."  So the field at $1 is converted and $1 moves on 48
!     bits.  Printed p.72: "The accumulator is cleared and the converted
!     field is placed into it at the specified offset ... The sign bit
!     in the sign byte register is set according to the sign of the
!     data".  Offset 68 puts the integer's units bit at accumulator bit
!     59, the last fraction bit of a floating-point word, and the
!     exponent bits 0-11 are zero.
!   E+I, 48 (no dds: unnormalized, C22-6578 p.30 comment (c)) makes the
!     exponent 48: the accumulator is now the integer N as an
!     unnormalized floating-point number.
!   ST(N), 0($2) stores it normalized; *(N), $L squares it ($L is
!     address 8.0); +, SUM / ST(U), SUM accumulate.
!   CBR+, $2, LOOP: add 1.0 to the value, count down, branch while the
!     count is not zero, and refill from the refill address when it is:
!     XW2's refill field is "$", XW2 itself, so $2 is (FLOAT, 25) again.
!   SRT, ROOT: STORE ROOT, printed p.94-95.
!   LOOP2 divides each stored Fk by the root.
!
! DATA.  Twenty-five integers, some negative, whose squares add up to
! 4**12 = 16,777,216, so the root is exactly 4096 and every quotient
! N/4096 is exact -- only the exponent changes:
!      1    -2     3  1024  -512   768   100   -99     7  1234
!   -321     5    64  -640    17   250   -33    11   400    -8
!    129  1000  1511 -2132  2179
!   Squares, by rows: 1 + 4 + 9 + 1048576 + 262144 + 589824 + 10000 +
!   9801 + 49 + 1522756 = 3443164;  103041 + 25 + 4096 + 409600 + 289 +
!   62500 + 1089 + 121 + 160000 + 64 = 740825;  16641 + 1000000 +
!   2283121 + 4545424 + 4748041 = 12593227.  3443164 + 740825 +
!   12593227 = 16777216.
!
! THE EXPECTED VALUES ARE HAND-DERIVED.  Every partial sum is an integer
! below 2**48, so every step is exact:
!   SUM  = 2**24 = .1 x 2**25             0328000000000000
!   ROOT = 2**12 = .1 x 2**13             01A8000000000000
!     (exponent 25 is odd: one is added and the fraction shifted right,
!     .01 x 2**26; the root of .01 is .1 and half of 26 is 13)
!   FLOAT+k = N(k)/4096: N(k)'s own normalized fraction and sign, with
!   an exponent of (number of bits in N(k)) - 12.  For example
!     1/4096      .1 x 2**-11             0178000000000000
!     -2/4096     -.1 x 2**-10            0158000000000008
!     1234/4096   .10011010010 x 2**-1    0039A40000000000
!     -2132/4096  -.100001010100 x 2**0   0008540000000008
!   All twenty-five are in tests/run_tests.sh, and
!   tests/problem_3_expected.py (p38) asserts each equals N(k)/4096.
!   x1_after: $1's value has moved 25 x 48 = 1200 bits = 18 words and 48
!     bits from STRNG; its count and refill are XW1's, untouched (V+I
!     neither counts nor refills).
!   x2_after: LOOP2's CB+ ran the count from 25 to zero and the value
!     from FLOAT to FLOAT+25; the refill field is XW2's.
!
! THE PAGE'S COMMENT (a) is about the very first "+, SUM": SUM is a word
! of zero bits, an order-of-magnitude zero with exponent 0, and "In the
! present case the nonzeros all have larger exponents".  That is true
! of this data (the smallest square is 1 = .1 x 2**1) and of any
! nonzero integer.  A ZERO in the string is another matter and is not
! in this data: 0 x 0 keeps exponent 96, the sum so far is shifted
! right past the 48 bits, and the sum is lost.  COMMENT (b), that EPLUS
! could be taken out "without causing any damage", is tested by
! problem_3_8_no_eplus.strap: the model agrees with the page, the
! Reference Manual's text (printed p.87) does not, and which is right is
! not settled (docs/NEXT.md "C22-6578 CHAPTER 3" item 5).
!
! >>> ON THE MODEL TODAY THIS DECK'S ARITHMETIC CHECKS FAIL, AND THE
! FAULT IS THE MODEL'S. <<<  OBSERVED 2026-11-15: SUM came back
! 02EBA9C840000000 = 6,114,882, which is the squares of the seventeen
! positive integers (11,446,049) LESS the squares of the eight negative
! ones (5,331,167): "*(N), $L" on a negative accumulator made a negative
! square.  ROOT and all twenty-five FLOAT words follow it and fail too
! (27 of 27); x1_after, x2_after and the PC pass.  Reference Manual
! printed p.80: a floating-point operand at address 8 is "accumulator
! bit positions 0-59 and sign byte register bit positions 4-7"; the
! model reads accumulator bit 60 for the sign.  The four-statement
! reproducer is decks/problem_3_fp_address_8_sign.strap, and
! docs/NEXT.md "C22-6578 CHAPTER 3" item 4 describes it.
! tests/run_tests.sh registered this deck with the three checks that
! passed and carried the twenty-seven that did not as comments.  FIXED
! 2026-11-16 (bsv/StretchExecute.bsv fpLoc8Operand): all thirty are
! registered and pass, and removing the fix fails exactly the 27
! (decks/problem_3_fp_address_8_sign.strap's header, injection 1).
! problem_3_8_positive.strap is this deck with absolute values, which
! the fault does not touch: all 29 of its checks pass, and the data-side
! injection was made there.

NORMV   Z, SUM
        LX, $1, XW1
        LX, $2, XW2
LOOP    LCV(V+I)(D, 48,6), 0.48($1), 68
EPLUS   E+I, 48
        ST(N), 0($2)
        *(N), $L
        +, SUM
        ST(U), SUM
        CBR+, $2, LOOP
        SRT, ROOT
LOOP2   L(N), 0($2)
        /, ROOT
        ST(U), 0($2)
        CB+, $2, LOOP2
        BEW, $
XW1     XW, STRNG, 25, $
XW2     XW, FLOAT, 25, $
SUM     DRZ(N), (1)
ROOT    DRZ(N), (1)
! --- the deck's data ------------------------------------------------
STRNG   DD(D, 48, 6), 1, -2, 3, 1024, -512, 768, 100, -99, 7, 1234
        DD(D, 48, 6), -321, 5, 64, -640, 17, 250, -33, 11, 400, -8
        DD(D, 48, 6), 129, 1000, 1511, -2132, 2179
FLOAT   DR(N), (25)
        END, NORMV
